ABOUT/dialog driver blits (MGAVIDEO): reconstruct the save/restore blit path reached when the dialog
opens, faithful to the driver asm (re_out/fist_mga_image.bin).  Part of the ABOUT-open path (patch 129).

- 0fbc: `di=[0x724]; if word[di]==0xA000 { 2d6d; [0x794]=0x7c8; [0x796]=0x140; 0fe4; 2e12 }` -- Ghidra
  composed word[[0x724]] (di|hi<<16) as a host pointer -> base-loss, and dropped the rowtable setup +
  the 2e12 tail.
- 0fe4: RESTORE blit save-buffer -> framebuffer.  The `call 0xfe2` (=pop ax;ret) on the jns branch is an
  EARLY RETURN (flag sign-bit clear = nothing saved yet, first paint) -- Ghidra modeled it as a normal
  call then ran the base-lost copy loop -> crash.  Reconstructed in the offset model (same class as
  patch 113's 0f62).
